Subject: [PATCH] TVP: admit upstream basic visual bindings with Android platform instances

Retain the pinned Window/Layer/Font TJS member definitions while selecting
an Android platform backend for the M2 basic display contract. Desktop,
transition, media and unsupported drawing members fail explicitly. The
original implementation remains available without the build flag; only
the generated copy is patched. The Android backend supplies real bitmaps,
fonts, composition and input and does not create placeholder methods.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure; standard visual pixel/input/lifecycle instrumentation

